# One direct external dependency per line: <crate-name> <reason>.
# `crates/kernel` may only use `serde` and `serde_json` (canonical wire IR).
# `crates/harness` may use `serde` and `serde_json` + `hrn-kernel` only (zero IO/async crates).
# `crates/modules/*` use no external crate at all (serde, serde_json and tokio come through `hrn-kernel` and `hrn-edge-rt`),
# except `rusqlite` in `crates/modules/memory` (its own SQLite file).
# Other external crates are strictly confined to `crates/edge/*`, `crates/front/*`, `crates/bins/*`, and `xtask`.
aes-gcm AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption for sealed share links and live collab frames
arboard OS clipboard text and RGBA image read for TUI Ctrl+V image paste
base64 RFC 4648 base64 encoding/decoding for multimodal image attachments
bytes buffer type for hyper HTTP/SSE streaming bodies
clap CLI argument and subcommand parsing for the single hrn binary
clap_complete shell completion script generation for hrn completions <shell>
crossterm cross-platform Windows Terminal / WezTerm / Unix terminal backend
flate2 pure-Rust (miniz_oxide) inflate for zip/tar.gz/office reads in `read`; already in the tree via png
form_urlencoded RFC 6749 application/x-www-form-urlencoded encoding/decoding
getrandom OS CSPRNG for OAuth PKCE verifier and state (RFC 7636)
globset compiled glob pattern matching for file discovery tool
grep-matcher the `Matcher` trait of the in-process ripgrep engine: locates the match column inside an over-long line
grep-regex regex matcher backing in-process ripgrep search tool
grep-searcher in-process ripgrep line/context search engine
http shared HTTP request/response types
http-body streaming body trait for hyper
http-body-util streaming body combinators for hyper
hyper HTTP/1.1 + HTTP/2 outbound client and loopback daemon server
hyper-util tokio IO glue and connection pooling for hyper
ignore gitignore-aware parallel directory walker for grep and glob
image pure-Rust PNG/JPEG/WebP/GIF/BMP decoding, resizing, and encoding for multimodal tools and TUI preview
percent-encoding URL query and path encoding/decoding
portable-pty ConPTY (Windows) / openpty (Unix) pseudo-terminals for `bash` with `pty: true`; safe API, ~30 KB source
process-wrap child-wrapper traits, CREATE_NO_WINDOW flags and Unix ProcessGroup (its snapshot-based Win32 JobObject is disabled: ~135 ms per spawn)
pulldown-cmark CommonMark parser for custom TUI markdown renderer
ratatui terminal UI layout and widget framework
rusqlite bundled SQLite (WAL) for DAG session persistence and the memory module's FTS5 store
rustls pure-Rust TLS client (ring backend)
rustls-platform-verifier OS native certificate store verification (Windows Cert Store + Linux)
serde serialization/deserialization for canonical IR, config, and wire payloads
serde_json JSON encoding/decoding for LLM wire protocols, tool schemas, and MCP JSON-RPC
sha2 FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 hashing for OAuth2 PKCE S256 and subscription request shaping
similar Myers/patience diff engine for `edit` unified diffs and TUI rendering
tokio async runtime, channels, timers, and process IO
tokio-rustls async TLS stream adapter for hyper
toml typed configuration parsing
toml_edit comment-preserving TOML editor for hrn config set/reset, preset saves, and provider setup
unicode-width terminal display width of text for TUI wrapping, truncation and cursor placement
win32job safe Win32 job objects: per-tree kill-on-close job and hrn-wide kill-on-close job without unsafe and without process-wrap's all-threads snapshot
ast-grep-core AST pattern matching and rewriting engine behind `ast_grep` / `ast_edit`
tree-sitter-rust Rust grammar for the ast tools
tree-sitter-python Python grammar for the ast tools
tree-sitter-javascript JavaScript grammar for the ast tools
tree-sitter-typescript TypeScript and TSX grammars for the ast tools
tree-sitter-go Go grammar for the ast tools
tree-sitter-json JSON grammar for the ast tools
tree-sitter-bash Bash grammar for the ast tools
